The conversion at 32°C (your tropical ambient):

H₂O Mass Fraction → Relative Humidity
X_H₂O	Humidity ratio ω	p_w (Pa)	p_sat at 32°C (Pa)	RH
1.5%	0.01523 kg/kg	2,421	4,759	~51%
2.4%	0.02459 kg/kg	3,852	4,759	~81%

The Math
Step 1:  ω = X_H2O / (1 - X_H2O)
Step 2:  p_w = ω × p_atm / (0.622 + ω)
Step 3:  p_sat(32°C) = 611.2 × exp(17.67 × 32 / 275.5) ≈ 4759 Pa
Step 4:  RH = p_w / p_sat

Model	X_H₂O	RH at 32°C	Label
Media.Air (dry tropical)	1.5%	~51% RH	Low humidity baseline
Media.TropicalAir (humid tropical)	2.4%	~81% RH	Malaysian equatorial conditions
Note: The 1.5% H₂O default in Media.Air was originally set for ISO 15°C, where it would actually be supersaturated (~142% RH — physically impossible as pure vapour). ThermoPower uses it as a generic modelling reference, not a true atmospheric condition. At 32°C, it translates to a realistic ~51% RH.
